  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">AbleChildAfrica - Organisational Development Grant 2011</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">AbleChildAfrica has been working for 4 years now with a wider remit than the former USDC UK - supporting a range of partners working on innovative solutions to change the lives of disabled children in Africa. Our 2007-2012 strategy has seen us achieving our goal of developing five partnerships accross 3 countries and finding a way to develop a positive approach to partnership with organisations working with disabled children and youth. We are coming to the end of our intial five year strategy and would like this grant to support the development of our next strategic plan consolidating what has been achieved to date and capitalising on our core mission going forward. In addition we would like support in two areas which we think will be key in that strategy - 1. the development of a well considered mechanism through which we can support mainstream development providers working with children to make their programmes and organisations inclusive and 2. the strengthening of our partnership network enabling it to grow and develop cross-network learning which we believe has significant benefits but which is difficult to fund from other sources.</narrative>
  </description>
